{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "Inclusion criterion 2 requires chronic hand and foot dermatitis diagnosed at least 3 years prior to screening for adults, but Section 3.1 (page 37) states chronic disease is defined as disease present for at least 6 months prior to screening, creating an inconsistency in the definition of chronic disease.",
      "page": 46,
      "quote": "Patients with chronic hand and foot dermatitis diagnosed at least 3 years prior to the screening visit for patients ≥18 years old, and at least 1 year prior to the screening visit for patients ≥12 to <18 years old.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "The protocol states that patients will be allowed rescue treatment with high potency TCS on hand/foot and/or systemic immunosuppressants (page 43), but also states that the use of topical and systemic medications for atopic chronic hand and foot dermatitis will be prohibited during the treatment period (page 43), which is contradictory.",
      "page": 43,
      "quote": "The use of topical and systemic medications for the treatment of atopic chronic hand and foot dermatitis will be prohibited during the treatment period. However, patients will be allowed to use topical medications for AD on parts of the body other than hand and foot. These topical medications will be limited to low to medium potency TCS creams. Moreover, patients will be advised to either a) use gloves or use tongue depressors while applying these creams if self-applying or b) have a caregiver apply these treatments. If medically necessary (ie, to control disease flares), rescue treatment in the form of high potency TCS on hand/foot and/or systemic immunosuppressants may be provided to study patients at the discretion of the investigator.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "The protocol states that randomization will be stratified by age (adults vs. adolescents), disease severity (IGA hand and foot 3 vs. 4), and geographic region (page 37 and 43), but the study design section (page 42) does not mention stratification, and the randomization section (page 43) repeats the same stratification, which is not an error per se, but the inconsistency is that the study design section (page 42) does not mention stratification, which is a minor omission.",
      "page": 42,
      "quote": "This is a global, multicenter, randomized, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study investigating the efficacy and safety of dupilumab monotherapy in adult and adolescent patients with moderate-to-severe atopic hand and foot dermatitis.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "The protocol states that the number of patients with hands only involvement will be capped at approximately 100 (page 42 and 46), but the total sample size is approximately 130, and the cap for adults is approximately 100, so the cap for hands only involvement is not clearly defined in relation to the total, and it is possible that the cap for hands only involvement could be higher than the total number of patients, which is illogical.",
      "page": 42,
      "quote": "The number of patients with hands only involvement will be capped at approximately 100.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "The protocol states that the primary endpoint is the proportion of patients achieving an IGA (hand and foot) score of 0 or 1 at week 16 (page 40), but the study design section (page 44) states that the end of treatment visit will occur at week 16, 2 weeks after the last dose of study drug, and the primary endpoint will be assessed at this visit, which is consistent, but the protocol does not specify the analysis population for the primary endpoint (e.g., intention-to-treat), which is a missing information.",
      "page": 40,
      "quote": "Proportion of patients achieving an IGA (hand and foot) score of 0 or 1 at week 16",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "The protocol states that the study will include adult and adolescent patients (page 42), but the inclusion criteria (page 46) state that patients must be ≥12 years old, which is consistent, but the protocol does not specify the upper age limit for adults, which is a minor omission.",
      "page": 46,
      "quote": "Male or female ≥12 years old at time of the screening visit.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "The protocol states that the screening period has a minimum duration of 4 weeks and maximum up to 8 weeks (page 42), but the inclusion criterion 12 (page 48) requires patients to have been compliant with skin protection measures through the entire duration of the screening period (minimum of 4 weeks but lasting to a maximum of 8 weeks), which is consistent, but the protocol does not specify the exact duration of the screening period for each patient, which is a minor omission.",
      "page": 42,
      "quote": "Screening period (minimum duration of 4 weeks and maximum up to 8 weeks)",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "The protocol states that the study will exclude patients with other dermatides (page 37), but the exclusion criteria (page 48) only exclude patients with a positive patch test reaction to one or more allergens that is deemed clinically relevant, and do not explicitly exclude patients with other dermatides such as irritant contact dermatitis or allergic contact dermatitis, which is a contradiction.",
      "page": 37,
      "quote": "Given the unclear scientific rationale for dupilumab in forms of hand and foot dermatitis other than atopic hand and foot dermatitis, as well as the variable results reported in the literature of the effect of dupilumab on ACD, the patient population in this study will exclude patients with these other dermatides.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "The protocol states that the study will include patients with moderate-to-severe forms of disease (IGA hands and feet of 3 or 4) (page 37), but the inclusion criteria (page 46) require patients to have an IGA hand and foot score of 3 or 4 at screening and baseline, which is consistent, but the protocol does not specify how the IGA score will be assessed (e.g., by a trained assessor), which is a minor omission.",
      "page": 37,
      "quote": "Limiting the study population with moderate-to-severe forms of disease (Investigator Global Assessment [IGA] hands and feet of 3 or 4)",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "The protocol states that the study will have a 12-week follow-up period (page 37), but the study design section (page 44) states that the end of study visit will occur at week 28, which is consistent (16 weeks treatment + 12 weeks follow-up), but the protocol does not specify the duration of the follow-up period for patients who prematurely discontinue study drug, which is a minor omission.",
      "page": 37,
      "quote": "The 12-week follow-up period is based on the expected pharmacokinetics (PK) of dupilumab after the last dose",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "The protocol states that the study will be conducted in response to COVID-19 (page 39), but the protocol does not specify any specific COVID-19-related procedures or modifications, which is a minor omission.",
      "page": 39,
      "quote": "Study Conduct in Response to COVID-19",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "The protocol states that the study will have a blinded, randomized, placebo-controlled design (page 37), but the study design section (page 42) does not mention blinding, which is a minor omission.",
      "page": 37,
      "quote": "A blinded, randomized, placebo-controlled design is chosen to minimize bias in data collection and result interpretation.",
      "severity": "minor"
    }
  ]
}
